		<div class="concept-text">
			<h4 style="color: var(--teal)">Reversible Action</h4>
			<p>DAWZY's design refuses the brittle pattern in which an LLM rewrites the project file directly. Each request is compiled into a Lua ReaScript that ReaPy executes against live session state, and every script is constructed so its effect can be reversed with a single undo. We posit that this is the load-bearing safety primitive of the system. A probabilistic generator, sitting in front of a deterministic editor, can only be trusted if the editor preserves a path back to the previous state.</p>
		</div>
	</div>

