		<div class="concept-text">
			<h4 style="color: var(--orange)">MCP as Interop Layer</h4>
			<p>DAWZY exposes three Model Context Protocol tools to the LLM, namely a state query that enumerates tracks, items, FX, and routing; an FX parameter setter that translates human units (dB, ms) into ReaScript slider ranges; and a local invocation of MusicGen-small for generated audio. The salient design move is that unit translation is handled by a tool rather than by the model. The authors report that GPT-5 reliably failed at converting between dB and the 0-to-1 slider range that REAPER's plugin API expects, and so they removed the responsibility from the LLM entirely.</p>
		</div>
	</div>

