			<h4 style="color: var(--violet)">Concurrent Action</h4>
			<p>The central finding of Son et al. is empirical rather than conceptual. Across 214 turns of professional designers working with their second probe system, concurrent action (the user editing the artifact while the agent edits the same artifact) appeared in 31.8% of turns. Five distinct concurrent patterns are reported, including <em>in-situ co-editing</em>, <em>artifact takeover</em>, and <em>demonstration-based steering</em>. We note that no current music-AI agent system, DAWZY included, has an architectural slot for this category of behavior, because no current music-AI agent system can perceive simultaneous user modifications to the artifact it is editing.</p>
		</div>
	</div>

